# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_per_tenant_cap.py" "CO-CHANGE PER-TENANT CAP GATE: PASS" "co-change pool PER-(account,repo) MEMORY GUARD (orthogonal to the per-account fairness cap; Round-2 concurrency follow-up)" "co-change pool MEMORY guard (Round-2 concurrency follow-up): the per-account fairness cap (VERIPSA_PER_ACCOUNT_COCHANGE_CAP, default 50) protects against a tenant flooding ACROSS repos but does NOT bound concurrent clones of the SAME repo -- a tenant rapid-pushing one monorepo / webhook redelivery storm targeting one repo can pile many in-flight + queued tasks of the SAME (account, repo) up to the per-account cap, each clone allocating its own tempdir on the small free-tier memory. THE FIX adds an orthogonal per-(account, repo) cap VERIPSA_COCHANGE_PER_TENANT_CAP (default 3, kill switch =0). Past it a new submit is DROPPED CONTENT-FREE + FAIL-OPEN (advisory 2nd signal, self-heals on next push) -- the same shape as the existing per-account cap drop. Implementation: a tiny dict tenant_counts[(account, repo)] = in-flight + queued count, guarded by a lock so the check + increment in submit and the decrement in the worker do NOT race; the slot covers BOTH queued and in-flight time so the cap is about CONCURRENT clone tempdirs (the memory cost) not just queued items. A cap of 0 disables the gate (zero-overhead kill-switch path); kwarg repo=None on submit() bypasses the gate too (legacy in-test submit shape still works). Behaviour-preserving for the non-flooding case (same return shapes, same fail-open + content-free guarantees); only adds an extra drop path on a single (account, repo) past 3 concurrent clones. This gate proves it scheduler-level, DB-free + clone-free (deterministic, not a timing race): (a) PER-TENANT CAP DROPS -- ONE (account, repo) past cap=3 drops content-free + fail-open (no raise, the dropped Future carries the per-tenant marker), while a DIFFERENT repo for the SAME account is still accepted (per-(account, repo) granularity) AND a DIFFERENT account on the same repo path is still accepted; (b) SLOT RELEASED ON COMPLETION -- the cap is in-flight + queued, NOT a permanent quota; after a burst COMPLETES the second burst on the same (account, repo) is accepted again; (c) KILL SWITCH -- per_tenant_cap=0 disables the per-(account, repo) gate entirely (only the per-account fairness cap remains active); (d) CAP KNOB -- env_int min_value=0 so a 0 is the intentional disable (not a refusal) while a NEGATIVE value is still refused LOUDLY at startup; (e) PER-ACCOUNT CAP STILL WORKS -- the new gate is additive, not a replacement: the existing per-account fairness cap still drops content-free when the per-tenant gate is disabled. content-free throughout" "co-change per-(account, repo) memory cap (Round-2 follow-up): VERIPSA_COCHANGE_PER_TENANT_CAP (default 3, =0 to disable) bounds in-flight + queued clones per (account, repo) so a tenant flooding ONE repo cannot allocate many concurrent clone tempdirs on the small free-tier memory; over-cap submits drop content-free + fail-open (never raise) -- same shape as the per-account cap drop; additive on top of VERIPSA_PER_ACCOUNT_COCHANGE_CAP, content-free" 24
